# Project rules: OpenCRVS NIMS demo

- Target is OpenCRVS core v2.1.x (see OPENCRVS_CORE_IMAGE_TAG). Never rely on memory for OpenCRVS APIs, config keys, scopes or folder names.
- Before writing code, read the docs at documentation.opencrvs.org (technical/guides) and the types inside node_modules/@opencrvs/toolkit. If you cannot find something, say so and stop. Do not invent.
- Never invent real-world data (LGA names, office names, NINs). Use only data files I supply. Mark all demo data as demo.
- Small steps. One concern per commit. Show me the diff plan before large edits.
- After every change, append 3 to 5 lines to LEARNING_LOG.md: what changed, which file, why, how I verify it.
- Follow the template's existing patterns before adding new ones.
- No secrets in git. Use .env.example and Kubernetes Secrets.
- Write tests for every new service function. TypeScript strict mode.
- Plain, short README and comments. No marketing language.
- Do not start extra work until asked. One concern at a time.
